  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Disabling \"read/write enabled\" on a mesh should, normally, reduce memory usage, and therefore should be encouraged. Currently however it forces avatars to be ranked as very poor - presumably because the mesh data is discarded before the polygons can be counted.\n\nAs a limitation this is fine, but to avoid confusion, the option should be forced on by the SDK, or ideally by the client on load, to avoid people being confused about why their avatar is marked as very poor all of a sudden.",
